Subject: [PATCH] http: with a SID, descramble only the chosen service

recpt1 fed the whole transport stream to libarib25 and split by SID
afterwards, so MULTI2 ran on every scrambled packet of the multiplex.  On
a slow CPU (the ~400 MHz single-core MIPS of these devices) that is the
bottleneck: one service already needs almost the whole core, and a
multi-service BS/CS multiplex cannot be descrambled in real time.

Run the splitter first when a SID is given, then descramble what is left.
The splitter keeps the chosen service's PAT (rebuilt), PMT, PCR, ECM
(the program_info CA_descriptor PID) and ES, which is all libarib25 needs
to get the key and descramble -- so MULTI2 now runs on one service's
packets, not the whole multiplex.  Without a SID the whole stream is
descrambled, as before.

At end of session the decoder was fed the split stream, so its flushed
output is already the chosen service: write it without splitting again.

---
diff --git a/recpt1/recpt1.c b/recpt1/recpt1.c
index eca3ab6..8d9f032 100644
--- a/recpt1/recpt1.c
+++ b/recpt1/recpt1.c
@@ -346,17 +346,6 @@ reader_func(void *p)
 
         buf = sbuf; /* default */
 
-        if(use_b25) {
-            code = b25_decode(dec, &sbuf, &dbuf);
-            if(code < 0) {
-                fprintf(stderr, "b25_decode failed (code=%d). fall back to encrypted recording.\n", code);
-                use_b25 = FALSE;
-            }
-            else
-                buf = dbuf;
-        }
-
-
         if(use_splitter) {
             splitbuf.buffer_filled = 0;
 
@@ -413,6 +402,19 @@ reader_func(void *p)
             ;
         } /* if */
 
+        /* Descramble after the splitter: with a SID only the chosen service
+         * is left (its PAT/PMT/PCR/ECM/ES), so MULTI2 runs on far fewer
+         * packets.  Without a SID, buf is the whole stream (as before). */
+        if(use_b25) {
+            code = b25_decode(dec, &buf, &dbuf);
+            if(code < 0) {
+                fprintf(stderr, "b25_decode failed (code=%d). fall back to encrypted recording.\n", code);
+                use_b25 = FALSE;
+            }
+            else
+                buf = dbuf;
+        }
+
 
         if(!fileless) {
             /* write data to output file */
@@ -468,6 +470,8 @@ reader_func(void *p)
             buf.size = 0;
 
             if(use_b25) {
+                /* the decoder was fed the split stream, so its flushed
+                 * output is already the chosen service */
                 code = b25_finish(dec, &sbuf, &dbuf);
                 if(code < 0)
                     fprintf(stderr, "b25_finish failed\n");
@@ -475,22 +479,6 @@ reader_func(void *p)
                     buf = dbuf;
             }
 
-            if(use_splitter) {
-                /* 分離対象以外をふるい落とす */
-                code = split_ts(splitter, &buf, &splitbuf);
-                if(code == TSS_NULL) {
-                    split_select_finish = TSS_ERROR;
-                    fprintf(stderr, "PMT reading..\n");
-                }
-                else if(code != TSS_SUCCESS) {
-                    fprintf(stderr, "split_ts failed\n");
-                    break;
-                }
-
-                buf.data = splitbuf.buffer;
-                buf.size = splitbuf.buffer_filled;
-            }
-
             if(!fileless && !file_err) {
                 wc = write(wfd, buf.data, buf.size);
                 if(wc < 0) {
